<section class="section paper" id="intelligence">
<div class="section-head"><div class="kicker">INGREDIENT INTELLIGENCE</div><h2>Build with purpose.</h2><p class="section-lede">LEAN BLEND uses food-first ingredients with useful nutritional roles. “Support” language is intentional: smoothies are not medicines.</p></div>
<div class="goal-grid" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr)">
<div class="callout"><h3>GINGER</h3><p>Distinctive flavour and a long history of use for digestive comfort. Start with a small amount.</p></div>
<div class="callout"><h3>CHIA + FLAX</h3><p>Dense sources of fibre and useful fats. Increase portions gradually if your usual fibre intake is low.</p></div>
<div class="callout"><h3>BERRIES</h3><p>Whole-fruit sources of fibre and polyphenols, with strong flavour at relatively modest portions.</p></div>
<div class="callout"><h3>KEFIR</h3><p>Fermented dairy option for people who tolerate it; useful as a creamy smoothie base.</p></div>
<div class="callout"><h3>OATS</h3><p>Whole-grain carbohydrate and fibre that can make a smoothie more substantial.</p></div>
<div class="callout"><h3>CITRUS</h3><p>Excellent for brightness and vitamin C, but not appropriate for everyone who prefers a gentler or lower-acid option.</p></div>
</div>
<div class="builder-tip"><b>LEAN BLEND rule:</b> more of an ingredient is not automatically better. Fibre, caffeine, citrus and strong spices should be adjusted to individual tolerance.</div>
</section>
<section class="section paper" id="principles"><div class="section-head"><div class="kicker">LEAN BLEND STANDARD</div><h2>Useful nutrition.<br/>No hype.</h2><p class="section-lede">Protein and fibre can support fullness, while hydration supports fluid intake. LEAN BLEND does not present any smoothie as a magic fat burner, detox or hangover cure.</p></div><div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:18px"><div class="callout"><h3>300 ML</h3><p>One consistent serving target across the entire collection.</p></div><div class="callout"><h3>HOME COST</h3><p>Ingredient consumption only. No commercial cost layers.</p></div><div class="callout"><h3>LABEL CHECK</h3><p>Nutrition figures remain engineering estimates until final package-label verification.</p></div></div></section>
